setting up a UI session to run the c++ file

setting up a make file (step 2, optional if already exists):
 - set up the CMakeLists.txt file, this contains all information for the cmake to run (see above link for more information on the CMakeLists.txt file
 - we have a separate *build* directory (where the buildscripts are generated and run) and *source* directory (where the sources/code resides, where the .cc file is), we want them in the same file directory
 - if getting file does not exist, check to see if step 1 has been run in this instance of the terminal
- if any changes are made to the CMake file, this will cause issues with compilation into the build directory, need to delete cache before remaking

##
cd [FILE_DIRECTORY_CONTAINING_SOURCE_DIRECTORY]
mkdir [NAME]_Build
cd [BUILD_DIRECTORY]
cmake -DCMAKE_PREFIX_PATH=/home/samuel/geant4-v11.4.2 [SOURCE_DIRECTORY]
make -j4
./[EXECUTABLE]
##

once edits have been done on the source file, we can just run 'make -j8' to update the executable
##
make -j8
##

to just run the file, simply do 
##
./[EXECUTABLE]
##



using the geant4 UI interface (QT)
- we can set up 'macro files' (see example B1) which allow us to set up specific visualisations

interactive mode:
    - uses GUI, we run single commands
    - simulates visually the results, takes longer to run

batch mode:
    - does not use GUI, runs off of a macro file (contains commands)
    - just outputs the results (takes in information from one file and outputs it to another)
    - ./[EXECUTABLE] [MACRO].mac

look at the example macro files and commands, very useful :D





